  "about": "A front door's derivations, one signed page and two padded boxes (#121, crypto/door.ts). HKDF-SHA-256 (RFC 5869, empty salt, 32 bytes) of the door's Ed25519 public key, or of a reply seed, from Python's hmac and hashlib; Ed25519 over the UTF-8 tag, one 0x00 byte and the page, and X25519, from Python's cryptography package; XChaCha20-Poly1305 as HChaCha20 from its raw ChaCha20 block then its ChaCha20Poly1305, checked against RFC 7748 and draft-irtf-cfrg-xchacha-03's vectors, then each box opened again with libsodium (PyNaCl). None is @noble. A padded box is box.ts's box of a body framed as a seal's is (a 4-byte big-endian length, the plaintext, then zeros), sized so the box is exactly one of the four blob sizes, with the mailbox id's UTF-8 as the AAD. The ephemeral secrets and nonces are fixed here only. Each key, id, page, plaintext, record and blob is its bytes, and a mailbox id is the unpadded base64url of its bytes; only the labels are text.",
